msgctxt "help/135/0"
msgid "Unrest"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/135/1"
msgid ""
"Even if you are very careful to provide for all the needs and desires "
"of your population, you should always monitor the level of discontent, "
"or Unrest, in your city. Unrest is the measure of your citizens' "
"satisfaction (or dissatisfaction) with you and the way you are "
"governing. Left unchecked, Unrest can lead to riots, which can cause "
"serious damage to your city.\n"
"Unrest is based on population tax, conscription rates, and "
"unemployment. As each of these increase, there is a chance that Unrest "
"will worsen. Naturally, your people will resent high taxes and high "
"conscription rates, and will demand a healthy economy with an abundance "
"of jobs. Unrest is also affected by your city's security. Do your best "
"to see that each area of     \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #138Next Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/136/0"
msgid "Employment"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/136/1"
msgid ""
"The employment rate of your city will be an important factor in "
"determining your population growth rate. An abundance of available jobs "
"will make people want to move to the city -- a high level of "
"unemployment will chase them away. You can find out the employment rate "
"of your city at any time by selecting Census from menu bar, or by going "
"to the Forum and consulting the Treasurer.\n"
"\n"
"Many of the structures you build on the City level will create "
"employment for your populace. A city's employment will increase "
"whenever any of the following structures are built: \n"
"\n"
"Any Forum, Any place of Worship,Bath House, Praefecture, Barracks, "
"Grammaticus, Rhetor, Library,\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #140Next Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/137/0"
msgid "Illness"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/137/1"
msgid ""
"Like unrest, illness can appear in pockets throughout your city if "
"conditions favor it. Monitor the illness levels in your city by "
"checking the illness color overlay, which highlights areas of low, "
"medium, and high illness.\n"
"\n"
"Illness levels relate directly to the quality of your city's "
"sanitation. To minimize illness, you must provide sanitation in the "
"form of Bath Houses and Hospitals. Areas of housing with no access to a "
"Bath House are more likely to have high levels of illness, and a "
"hospital cover lower than 100 percent can worsen illness throughout "
"your city.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#57Previous Page# / #141Next Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/138/0"
msgid "Unrest (page 2)"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/138/1"
msgid ""
"your city is patrolled by soldiers from a barracks, or from a "
"praefecture. Such patrols can prevent riots and will quash them if they "
"do break out. Population tax, conscription, unemployment, and security "
"will work in conjunction to determine Unrest. A worsening of one can be "
"offset by an improvement in another. A hike in the population tax, for "
"example, might not heighten Unrest if it is offset by a lowering of "
"your conscription rate.\n"
"\n"
"You may monitor your city's level of Unrest by selecting Unrest from "
"the pull-down menu at the top of the tool box. Click on the legend "
"square and view your city map to see which areas show unrest.\n"
"If conditions favor unrest, it will appear in pockets in your city, and "
"it will spread. The color overlay will \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#135Previous Page# / #139Next Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/139/0"
msgid "Unrest (page 3)"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/139/1"
msgid ""
"display yellow, orange, and red spots on the city map to indicate low, "
"medium, and high levels of unrest. To reduce Unrest in your city, pay "
"close attention to your conscription rate, population tax, and "
"employment level. Can you afford to reduce taxes? Can your Legion bear "
"a reduction of the Conscription rate? Can you build more job-producing "
"structures in your city to boost employment?\n"
"\n"
"If you tend to all of the above factors and your city still has an "
"alarming level of Unrest, you may reduce Unrest by building Barracks "
"and Praefectures. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#138Previous Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/140/0"
msgid "Employment (page 2)"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/140/1"
msgid ""
"Any Entertainment structure, Hospital, Market, Business.\n"
"\n"
"The more advanced the structure is, the more jobs it will create. More "
"jobs mean more people; more people mean more tax dollars; more tax "
"dollars give you the ability to develop your city and raise Land "
"Values. High Land Values are the key to a thriving and successful city!\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#136Previous Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/141/0"
msgid "Illness (page 2)"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/141/1"
msgid ""
"If illness levels become too high, disease will break out. Disease "
"appears as skull-and-crossbones symbols on your city map. If left "
"unchecked, disease can spread. Disease will destroy housing and can "
"seriously damage surrounding land values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#137Previous Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

msgctxt "help/142/0"
msgid "Unrest (page 4)"
msgstr "SCHUTT"

msgctxt "help/142/1"
msgid ""
"Their presence alone will reduce Unrest in the areas surrounding them, "
"and the soldiers and vigiles they send out will cut Unrest for every "
"house they pass by while on patrol.\n"
"As a last resort, you always have the option to destroy any house that "
"turns up red under the Unrest display. Sometimes it is better to "
"\"eliminate\" troublemakers before they can do any real harm. If unrest "
"leads to a riot, soldiers from your barracks and vigiles from your "
"praefectures will automatically move to the troubled spot and try to "
"put down the riot.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#139Previous Page#"
msgstr "Zu diesem Thema gibt es keine wichtigen Informationen."

