msgctxt "help/295/0"
msgid "Help with Gardens"
msgstr "Hilfe bei Gärten"

msgctxt "help/295/1"
msgid ""
"Building Gardens and Plazas will boost land values by providing "
"pleasant public places for your citizens. They will also help you to "
"raise your Culture rating. Sections of  Plaza also serve as sections of "
"road. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#296Tips# / #297History#"
msgstr ""
"Der Bau von Gärten und Plätzen läßt den Landwert steigen, da der "
"Bevölkerung damit angenehme öffentliche Einrichtungen zur Verfügung "
"stehen. Auch Ihre Kultur-Wertung steigt dadurch. Plätze dienen auch als "
"Teile von Straßen. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#296Tips# / #297Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/296/0"
msgid "Tips for Amenities"
msgstr "Tips für Einrichtungen"

msgctxt "help/296/1"
msgid ""
"Use gardens and plazas to improve land values around housing.  In "
"harder provinces or skill levels, they are a good way to keep tents "
"from disappearing.\n"
"\n"
"Place plazas with care, as your city's walkers are sometimes likely to "
"wander aimlessly around them. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#295Help# / #297History#"
msgstr ""
"Benutzen Sie Gärten und Plätze, um den Landwert in Wohngegenden zu "
"steigern. In schwierigeren Provinzen oder höheren Schwierigkeitsgraden "
"sind sie sehr nützlich, damit die Zelte nicht wieder verschwinden.\n"
"\n"
"Bauen Sie Ihre Plätze mit Bedacht, da die Fußgänger sonst ziellos "
"darauf herumlaufen. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#295Hilfe# / #297Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/297/0"
msgid "Roman Gardens"
msgstr "Römische Gärten"

msgctxt "help/297/1"
msgid ""
"Romans of all classes were in love with the country life, and wherever "
"possible sought to bring a little of it into the city itself.  As of  "
"270 AD, a full 7% of the city was covered by some kind of garden. Every "
"domus had its private interior garden, carefully groomed and maintained "
"by the house slaves.  The public gardens, called horti, were property "
"of the Emperor and used as parks.  These tiny pieces of rustica were "
"elaborately sculptured, though their designers attempted to strike a "
"balance between architectural elegance and the simple beauty of nature. "
" Flowers and aromatic herbs were grown in artistically arranged beds, "
"bushes and trees were cut and shaped into the forms of animals, and "
"artifical pools, \n"
"\n"
"#298Next Page#\n"
"#295Help#/#296Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Römer aller Klassen liebten das Landleben und versuchten, wo immer "
"möglich, etwas davon in die Stadt mitzubringen. Seit 270 n.Chr. waren "
"volle 7% der Stadt mit Gärten aller Art bedeckt. Jeder Domus hatte "
"seinen privaten Garten im Innenhof, der von den Haussklaven sorgsam "
"gehegt und gepflegt wurde. Die öffentlichen Gärten, Horti genannt, "
"gehörten dem Imperator und wurden als Parks benutzt. Diese kleinen "
"Oasen des Landlebens waren kunstvoll arrangiert, obwohl ihre Designer "
"versuchten, ein Gleichgewicht zwischen architektonischer Eleganz und "
"natürlicher Einfachheit zu treffen.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#298Nächste Seite#\n"
"#295Hilfe#/#296Tips#"

msgctxt "help/298/0"
msgid "Roman Gardens (cont.)"
msgstr "Röm. Gärten (Forts.)"

msgctxt "help/298/1"
msgid ""
"waterfalls, and canals were constructed.  A few gardens had a portico, "
"a porch-like structure running around the outside wall so that the "
"garden could be enjoyed even in rain or the heat of the summer sun. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#297Previous Page#\n"
"#295Help#/#296Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Blumen und duftende Kräuter wuchsen in künstlerisch angelegten Beeten, "
"Büsche und Bäume wurden getrimmt und in Tierform gebracht, und "
"künstliche Teiche, Wasserfälle und Kanäle durchzogen das Gelände. "
"Einige Gärten besaßen einen Säulengang, eine Art überdachte Veranda, "
"die um die Außenwand lief, damit der Besucher den Garten sogar im Regen "
"oder in der Sommersonnenhitze genießen konnte. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#297Vorige Seite#\n"
"#295Hilfe#/#296Tips#"

