msgctxt "help/325/0"
msgid "Help with Plazas"
msgstr "Hilfe bei Plätzen"

msgctxt "help/325/1"
msgid ""
"Building Gardens and Plazas will boost land values by providing "
"pleasant public places for your citizens. They will also help you to "
"raise your Culture rating. Sections of  Plaza also serve as sections of "
"road.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#326Tips# / #327History#"
msgstr ""
"Der Bau von Gärten und Plätzen läßt den Landwert steigen, da der "
"Bevölkerung damit angenehme öffentliche Einrichtungen zur Verfügung "
"stehen. Auch Ihre Kultur-Wertung steigt dadurch. Plätze dienen auch als "
"Teile von Straßen.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#326Tips# / #327Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/326/0"
msgid "Tips for Amenities"
msgstr "Tips für Einrichtungen"

msgctxt "help/326/1"
msgid ""
"Use gardens and plazas to improve land values around housing.  In "
"harder provinces or skill levels, they are a good way to keep tents "
"from disappearing.\n"
"\n"
"Place plazas with care, as your city's walkers are sometimes likely to "
"wander aimlessly around them. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#325Help# / #327History#"
msgstr ""
"Benutzen Sie Gärten und Plätze, um den Landwert in Wohngegenden zu "
"steigern. In schwierigeren Provinzen oder höheren Schwierigkeitsgraden "
"sind sie sehr nützlich, damit die Zelte nicht wieder verschwinden.\n"
"\n"
"Bauen Sie Ihre Plätze mit Bedacht, da die Fußgänger sonst ziellos "
"darauf herumlaufen. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#325Hilfe# / #327Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/327/0"
msgid "Roman Plazas"
msgstr "Römische Plätze"

msgctxt "help/327/1"
msgid ""
"The Column of Trajan\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#328Next Page#\n"
"#325Help#/#326Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Die Trajan-Säule\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#328Nächste Seite#\n"
"#325Hilfe#/#326Tips#"

msgctxt "help/328/0"
msgid "Roman Plazas"
msgstr "Römische Plätze"

msgctxt "help/328/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans built plazas in well-traveled public areas such as the Forum "
"Valley, and around important buildings such as major temples and the "
"Imperial palace.  Plazas were open areas paved with cut rock, sometimes "
"decorated with patterns of colored stone. Many of Rome's strictly "
"decorative monuments were located on plazas, particularly the victory "
"columns and arches earned by triumphant generals --  structures such as "
"the Column of Trajan, depicting the Emperor's conquest of the province "
"of Dacia, and the Arch of Septimius Severus, commemorating his "
"victories over the Parthians, Arabs, and Mesopotamians. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#327Previous Page#\n"
"#325Help#/#326Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Die Römer bauten Plätze in vielbesuchten öffentlichen Gebieten wie dem "
"Forum-Tal und um andere wichtige Gebäude wie die großen Tempel und den "
"kaiserlichen Palast. Plazas waren offene, mit Pflastersteinen "
"ausgelegte Areale, die manchmal mit Mustern aus farbigen Steinen "
"geschmückt waren. Viele von Roms der reinen Dekoration dienenden "
"Monumenten standen auf Plätzen, vor allem die Siegessäulen und -bögen "
"siegreicher Generäle - Bauwerke wie die Trajan-Säule, die die Eroberung "
"der Provinz Dakien durch den Imperator darstellt, oder den Bogen des "
"Septimius Severus, mit dem seine Siege über die Parther, Araber und "
"Mesopotamier verkündet wurden. \n"
"\n"
"#327Vorige Seite#\n"
"#325Hilfe#/#326Tips#"

