msgctxt "help/385/0"
msgid "Fountains"
msgstr "Brunnen"

msgctxt "help/385/1"
msgid ""
"Fountains create the largest area of water supply. A fountain must be "
"placed within a reservoir's zone of pipe access. It will then use the "
"pipe access to create a usable water supply for the area around it. "
"Multiple fountains can draw from a single reservoir. Building a network "
"of fountains supplied by reservoirs is a very effective way of "
"supplying your city with water.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#386Tips# / #387History#"
msgstr ""
"Brunnen versorgen das größte Areal mit Wasser. Ein Brunnen muß im "
"Leitungsgebiet eines Reservoirs liegen. Damit kann der Brunnen das "
"umliegende Areal mit trinkbarem Wasser versorgen. Ein Anschluß mehrerer "
"Brunnen an ein Reservoir ist möglich. Eine effektive Methode, die Stadt "
"mit Wasser zu versorgen, besteht deshalb darin, ein Netz aus Brunnen zu "
"bauen, die von den Reservoirs versorgt werden.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#386Tips# / #387Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/386/0"
msgid "Tips for Fountains"
msgstr "Tips für Brunnen"

msgctxt "help/386/1"
msgid ""
"By building fountains at the farthest corners of a reservoir's area of "
"pipe access, you can cover a large square area with water supply.  "
"However, this doesn't mean that these are the most convenient locations "
"for fountains in your city. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#385Help# / #387History#"
msgstr ""
"Wenn Sie Brunnen an den äußersten Enden des Leitungsgebiets eines "
"Reservoirs bauen, können Sie ein großes Areal mit Wasser versorgen. "
"Diese Stellen müssen allerdings nicht unbedingt die praktischsten "
"Plazierungen für Brunnen sein ...  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#385Hilfe# / #387Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/387/0"
msgid "The Fountains of Rome"
msgstr "Die Brunnen von Rom"

msgctxt "help/387/1"
msgid ""
"The Trevi Fountain\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Next Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Der Brunnen von Trevi \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Nächste Seite#\n"
"#385Hilfe#/#386Tips#"

msgctxt "help/388/0"
msgid "Fountains"
msgstr "Brunnen"

msgctxt "help/388/1"
msgid ""
"From ancient times to the present, Rome has been famous for its "
"magnificent fountains.  Numerous songs and stories have been inspired "
"by their constant flow.  In ancient Rome, the fountains served a double "
"purpose  as sources of fresh water for the public and as works of art.  "
"The fountains were linked to reservoirs by a pipe network usually made "
"of ceramic, though the much more expensive lead was infrequently used.  "
"Carved wooden pipes also sometimes made an appearance.   \n"
"\n"
"The oldest fountain in Rome is a natural spring, the Lacus Juturnae in "
"the Forum valley.  New fountains were built as they were needed, or as "
"they were \n"
"#387Previous Page#/#389Next Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Seit seinen Ursprüngen bis in heutige Zeiten ist Rom berühmt für seine "
"prächtigen Brunnen. Ihr ständiges Plätschern inspirierte zu vielen "
"Liedern und Geschichten. Im alten Rom dienten die Brunnen einem "
"zweifachen Zweck: zur Frischwasserversorgung der Bevölkerung und als "
"Kunstwerke. Die Brunnen waren über ein Leitungsnetz, das zumeist aus "
"Keramik und seltener aus dem teuren Blei bestand, mit den Reservoirs "
"verbunden. Auch hölzerne Leitungen fanden hin und wieder Verwendung. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#387Vorige Seite#/#389Nächste Seite#\n"
"#385Hilfe#/#386Tips#"

msgctxt "help/389/0"
msgid "The Fountains of Rome (cont.)"
msgstr "Die Brunnen von Rom (Forts.)"

msgctxt "help/389/1"
msgid ""
"wanted -- fountains were often used as monuments to famous people or "
"events.  As of 270 AD, Rome had more than 1,200 public fountains.  \n"
"\n"
"One of the most famous fountains in Rome is the Trevi fountain, "
"originally constructed during ancient times but completely remodeled "
"and rebuilt in recent centuries.  This fountain, like many of Rome's "
"fountains, has a legend associated with it that says anyone who throws "
"a coin in the fountain is guaranteed a return to Rome.  Its waters come "
"from the Aqua Vergine, and have been considered the city's best-tasting "
"for centuries.  \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Previous Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Roms ältester Brunnen ist eine natürliche Quelle, der Lacus Juturnae im "
"Forum-Tal. Neue Brunnen wurden nach Bedarf gebaut, oder wenn sie "
"gewünscht wurden - sie dienten oft als Denkmäler für berühmte Leute "
"oder Ereignisse. Bereits im Jahr 270 n.Chr. besaß Rom mehr als 1200 "
"öffentliche Brunnen. \n"
"Einer der berühmtesten Brunnen von Rom ist der Brunnen von Trevi. Er "
"wurde bereits zu uralten Zeiten erbaut, in den letzten Jahrhunderten "
"jedoch mehrmals komplett neu gestaltet und neu gebaut. Auch mit diesem "
"Brunnen verbindet sich, wie mit so vielen Brunnen in Rom, eine Legende, "
"die besagt, daß jeder, der eine Münze in den Brunnen wirft, garantiert "
"noch einmal nach Rom zurückkehren wird. Sein Wasser, das Jahrhunderte "
"lang dafür berühmt war, den besten Geschmack aller Brunnen Roms zu "
"haben, erhält er von der Aqua Vergine. \n"
"#388Vorige Seite#\n"
"#385Hilfe#/#386Tips#"

