"#550Hilfe# / #552Geschichte#"

msgctxt "help/552/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus"
msgstr "Der röm. Circus"

msgctxt "help/552/1"
msgid ""
"The prescription of the writer Juvenal for a happy citizenry came down "
"to two essentials: \"Bread and Circuses.\"  Juvenal undoubtedly selected "
"circuses because the chariot races held in these buildings were the "
"most popular spectator sport in the city of Rome.  Charioteers were "
"organized into teams by color -- the Greens, the Blues, the Reds, and "
"the Whites -- and their standings were hotly contested and wagered on. "
"Successful chariot drivers had fan clubs who followed their careers.\n"
"\n"
"At its height, Rome had a total of four circuses. The undisputed king "
"of these was the Circus Maximus, located in the valley between the "
"Palatine and \n"
"#553Next Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Das Rezept für eine zufriedene Bevölkerung beschrieb der Schriftsteller "
"Juvenal mit zwei Worten: \"Brot und Circus\". Juvenal wählte den Circus "
"mit Bedacht aus, denn die in diesen Gebäuden abgehaltenen Wagenrennen "
"waren der populärste Zuschauersport in ganz Rom. Die Wagenlenker fuhren "
"in farblich bezeichneten Teams (die Grünen, die Blauen, die Roten und "
"die Weißen), ihr Rang war heiß umkämpft, und es wurden hohe Wetten auf "
"sie abgeschlossen. Erfolgreiche Wagenlenker hatten sogar Fanclubs, die "
"ihrer Karriere interessiert folgten.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#553Nächste Seite#\n"
"#550Hilfe#/#551Tips#"

msgctxt "help/553/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus (Cont.)"
msgstr "Der römische Circus (Forts.)"

msgctxt "help/553/1"
msgid ""
"Aventine hills. It was essentially complete as early as 329 BC, "
"although it was modified and added onto as time went by.  This huge "
"structure measured 654 by 218 yards, roughly the size of a dozen or so "
"football fields laid side by side. It could seat somewhere between "
"255,000 and 385,000 racing enthusiasts at a time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#552Previous Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""
"Zu seiner Blütezeit besaß Rom vier Zirkus-Bauten. Der unbestrittene "
"König dabei war der zwischen den Hügeln des Palatinus und des Aventinus "
"angesiedelt Circus Maximus. Er wurde bereits 329 v.Chr. in seiner "
"Grundausstattung fertiggestellt, jedoch im Laufe der Zeit ständig "
"verändert und vergrößert. Dieses riesige Bauwerk maß zirka 654 mal 218 "
"Meter, hatte also etwa die Größe von einem Dutzend nebeneinander "
"liegenden Football-Feldern. Zwischen 255000 und 385000 "
"Renn-Enthusiasten fanden darin bequeme Sitzplätze.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#552Vorige Seite#\n"
"#550Hilfe#/#551Tips#"

